    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d480">

                <pb facs="0577" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg493"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Sir
                            M. H. Herbert.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-02-13"><hi rendition="#italic">February 13,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 73.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that
                    the Senate, by its resolution of the 11th instant, two-thirds of the Senators
                    present concurring therein, gave its advice and consent, without amendment, to
                        <pb facs="0578" n="494" xml:id="pg494"/> the ratification of the convention
                    which I signed with you on January 24, 1903, providing for the settlement of the
                    questions between the United States and Great Britain with respect to the
                    boundary line between the Territory of Alaska and the British possessions in
                    North America.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
